# Lefthook Git Hooks Configuration

## Pre-commit Hook Rules

• Enable parallel execution for speed
• Format code automatically with staging
• Run comprehensive lint analysis
• Check for debugging statements removal
• Verify dependency health before commit
• Use conventional commit message format
• Fail on any quality issues

```yaml
pre-commit:
  parallel: true
  commands:
    dart-format:
      tags: quality
      glob: "**/*.dart"
      run: flutter format {staged_files} && git add {staged_files}
      stage_fixed: true
```

## Pre-push Hook Rules

• Run all unit tests before push
• Generate test coverage reports
• Use sequential execution for tests
• Update dependencies before testing
• Use expanded test reporter
• Verify coverage file generation

```yaml
pre-push:
  parallel: false
  commands:
    unit-tests:
      tags: test
      run: flutter test --coverage --reporter=expanded
```

## Debug Statement Prevention

• Block print() statements in lib/
• Block debugPrint() statements in lib/
• Allow debug statements in test files
• Provide clear failure messages
• Exit with error code one

```yaml
no-debug-prints:
  run: |
    if grep -r "print(" lib/ --include="*.dart" 2>/dev/null; then
      echo "❌ Found print() statements in lib/ directory"
      exit 1
    fi
```

## Commit Message Validation

• Enforce conventional commit format patterns
• Support standard prefixes: feat, fix, docs
• Allow optional scope in parentheses
• Require descriptive commit messages
• Block non-conforming commit attempts

```yaml
commit-msg:
  commands:
    conventional-commit:
      run: |
        if ! head -n1 {1} | grep -qE "^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore)(\(.+\))?: .+"; then
          exit 1
        fi
```

## Post-merge and Post-checkout

• Update IDE configurations automatically
• Run flutter pub get automatically
• Check for Flutter dependencies
• Ensure VS Code settings applied
• Update Android Studio configurations

```yaml
post-merge:
  commands:
    update-ide-config:
      run: |
        if [ -f ".vscode/settings.json" ]; then
          echo "VS Code settings updated"
        fi
```

## Output Configuration

• Include meta information in output
• Show summary of hook execution
• Display success messages clearly
• Report failure details comprehensively
• Skip meta output when silenced

```yaml
output:
  - meta
  - summary
  - success
  - failure
```

## Emergency Skip Options

• Use LEFTHOOK=0 for emergency commits
• Skip specific hooks when needed
• Maintain emergency override capability
• Document skip usage clearly
• Preserve team workflow standards